    "b-10-director-worker-the-worker-slice-is-the-4": {
      "id": "b-10-director-worker-the-worker-slice-is-the-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The worker slice is the primary live run agent surface. Board-level target\nadmission and wake-event handling are deterministic scheduler responsibilities;\nworker Pi sessions receive one claimed epoch target and work toward an exact\nmatch while the runner records durable evidence. The running phase also owns the\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "integration-resolver",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " agent, which is reserved for worker-output conflicts that\na serial merge cannot apply cleanly before PR handoff."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-director-worker-scheduler-delegation-5": {
      "id": "b-10-director-worker-scheduler-delegation-5",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Scheduler Delegation"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-director-worker-the-scheduler-chooses-ep-6": {
      "id": "b-10-director-worker-the-scheduler-chooses-ep-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The scheduler chooses epoch targets from durable state and graph-ranked board\nfeatures. It does not render a board-level prompt. The worker prompt receives\nthe target-local packet that was already admitted into the active epoch and\nclaimed by the runtime."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-director-worker-worker-slice-7": {
      "id": "b-10-director-worker-worker-slice-7",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Worker Slice"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-director-worker-the-worker-slice-builds-8": {
      "id": "b-10-director-worker-the-worker-slice-builds-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The worker slice builds prompts for one claimed epoch target. It carries the\ntarget packet, category-typed write-set rule, local regression requirements,\nselected worker context, resource map, optional repair request, and checkpoint-\nnote guidance. The handoff note can request a higher necessity rung with owner,\nobjdiff, and lower-rung failure evidence. The runner decides that request,\nexpands compile checks with the touched set, and records a\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "worker_checkpoints",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row with a tentative, confirmed, or regressed validation\nstate, then either continues the same worker session under the bounded attempt-\ntail policy or closes the paired "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worker_state",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
